Standing rules — Joystick Gremlin

Source of truth for Grok on this repo. Recall this file when asked.
Any change to rules is written here. Do not keep a second unofficial list.

1. Do not move large files. Edit files using copy/replace/paste and patch operations. Keep the structure of the program. Warn the user if a change could break a previous version.
2. Plan first. No code until you say go.
3. Announce every git push.
4. Branch: only Xbox_integration_ViGEmClient_dll for Xbox work. Optimization line stays on R15-OSC-Optimization. Do not mix Xbox commits onto Optimization unless you say merge.
5. Do not touch feature/osc-streamdeck unless you say so.
6. Stay on JoystickGremlin_, not JoystickGremlinEx_.
7. Warn before high CPU / memory / perf changes. Suggest cheaper options first.
8. You pull/fetch locally (GitHub Desktop). Pushes go through the GitHub API. You run with:
   poetry run python joystick_gremlin.py
   from E:\Users\Stacie\Documents\GitHub\JoystickGremlin_
9. Merge to “the program” only after you test.
10. Portable zip only, not a Program Files installer.
11. Do not reintroduce custom dill.dll loaders.
12. Do not commit ViGEmClient.dll to the repo from here (you already pushed it; that was your call).
13. Show generated / planned images before wiring new faces into QML, unless you already said go.
14. Xbox tab is labeled layout + incoming sources, not a DILL input device. Hardware maps with Map to Xbox.
15. Keep older R15 XML profiles loadable. Xbox-only nodes (map-to-xbox) are extra; stock R15 will not understand them.
16. Standing rules live in this file (grok_rules) at the program folder root. Recall from this file. Any rule change is written here.
17. All images generated for the user to view must be displayed in chat using image generation.
